<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna C-surface normalization: a single-statement if body drops its braces
    and prints the statement indented on the next line (user-reported
    readability issue on the angr fmt corpus binary; no upstream GH issue).

    Upstream Ghidra always braces the body.  kuna adds the settable option
    `braceelide` (DIV-37, docs/history.md), default-on: emit_block_if elides
    the braces when the then-body is a plain single-statement BlockCopy leaf
    (no label, no comment, exactly one printed op).  Labels, comments,
    multi-statement bodies, else arms, and loop/switch bodies keep braces;
    the `if (cond) goto L;` one-liner and `else if` collapse are unaffected.

    Stage model: S9 emission / brace-form policy.  P0 assertion:
    `option braceelide on|off`.

    be_fn (0x100000): int4 be_fn(int4 x) { if (x) return 7; return 3; }
      test edi,edi / jz +6 / mov eax,7 / ret / mov eax,3 / ret

    Pass 1 (default): the braceless form - `if (x)` with `return 7;` on the
    next line at one extra indent (assert #1, a 2-line chain, exactly once;
    the braced form cannot match because ` {` breaks the `$` anchor).
    Pass 2 (option braceelide off): the upstream braced `if (x) {`
    (assert #2, exactly once).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
85ff7406b807000000c3b803000000c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="be_fn"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern int4 be_fn(int4 x);</com>
  <com>lo fu be_fn</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option braceelide off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-BRACEELIDE #1: default renders the single-statement body braceless, indented (DIV-37)" min="1" max="1">if \(x\)$
^ {4}return 7;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CNORM-BRACEELIDE #2: braceelide off restores the upstream braced body" min="1" max="1">if \(x\) \{</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
